   "source": [
    "# Narrative analysis: hybrid-regime variation (Daniel)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Research question 2 (second half):** do hybrid regimes show greater annual score variation?\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook makes every number and the figure in my section of `NARRATIVE.md`. It reads the tables made by `build_data.py`, and runs that script first if the tables are missing."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "35765755",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-16T00:08:06.773018Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-11-16T00:08:06.772815Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-11-16T00:08:08.125323Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-11-16T00:08:08.124211Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "(2004, 9) 2011 to 2022\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import subprocess\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from scipy import stats\n",
    "\n",
    "ROOT = Path(\"..\")\n",
    "DATA = ROOT / \"data\"\n",
    "FIGS = Path(\"figures\")\n",
    "FIGS.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "if not (DATA / \"rq2_changes.csv\").exists():\n",
    "    subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"build_data.py\"], cwd=ROOT, check=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "changes = pd.read_csv(DATA / \"rq2_changes.csv\")\n",
    "panel = pd.read_csv(DATA / \"panel_country.csv\")\n",
    "rng = np.random.default_rng(418)\n",
    "\n",
    "REGIMES = [\"Authoritarian\", \"Hybrid regime\", \"Flawed democracy\", \"Full democracy\"]\n",
    "print(changes.shape, changes[\"year\"].min(), \"to\", changes[\"year\"].max())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "99a531de",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Measure: how much a country's score moves in a typical year\n",
    "\n",
    "`rq2_changes.csv` has 2,004 one-year changes (2010 to 2022, back-to-back years only). For each country I take the **mean absolute one-year change**, so a +0.3 and a -0.3 both count as 0.3 points of movement. Each country gets one number, so countries with more volatile years can't be counted twice.\n",
    "\n",
    "Countries are grouped by their **EIU regime in 2010**, the first year of the annual series, so the grouping is fixed before any of the changes happen."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "cf3b5fd6",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-16T00:08:08.127281Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-11-16T00:08:08.127098Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-11-16T00:08:08.745548Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-11-16T00:08:08.744670Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "                  countries  median  ci_low  ci_high\n",
      "regime_2010                                         \n",
      "Authoritarian            57   0.112   0.088    0.128\n",
      "Hybrid regime            31   0.150   0.107    0.185\n",
      "Flawed democracy         53   0.096   0.078    0.116\n",
      "Full democracy           26   0.063   0.050    0.076\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "changes[\"abs_change\"] = changes[\"score_change\"].abs()\n",
    "start = panel[panel[\"year\"] == 2010].set_index(\"country_code\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def by_country(df):\n",
    "    out = df.groupby(\"country_code\").agg(\n",
    "        mean_abs_change=(\"abs_change\", \"mean\"),\n",
    "        net_change=(\"score_change\", \"sum\"),\n",
    "        big_moves=(\"abs_change\", lambda s: (s >= 0.5).sum()),\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    out[\"regime_2010\"] = start[\"regime\"]\n",
    "    out[\"score_2010\"] = start[\"democracy_score\"]\n",
    "    out[\"country_name\"] = start[\"country_name\"]\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "countries = by_country(changes)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def boot_median(values, n=10000):\n",
    "    values = np.asarray(values)\n",
    "    meds = [np.median(rng.choice(values, len(values))) for _ in range(n)]\n",
    "    return np.percentile(meds, [2.5, 97.5])\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "summary = []\n",
    "for regime in REGIMES:\n",
    "    vals = countries.loc[countries[\"regime_2010\"] == regime, \"mean_abs_change\"]\n",
    "    low, high = boot_median(vals)\n",
    "    summary.append({\"regime_2010\": regime, \"countries\": len(vals), \"median\": vals.median(),\n",
    "                    \"ci_low\": low, \"ci_high\": high})\n",
    "summary = pd.DataFrame(summary).set_index(\"regime_2010\")\n",
    "print(summary.round(3))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "b2700846",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-16T00:08:08.747069Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-11-16T00:08:08.746860Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-11-16T00:08:09.102629Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-11-16T00:08:09.101447Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "hybrid median 0.150 vs all others 0.090; difference 0.060, 95% bootstrap CI [0.011 0.098]\n",
      "full democracy median: 0.063 | hybrid / full ratio: 2.4\n",
      "Mann-Whitney U, hybrid vs Authoritarian: U = 1105, two-sided p = 0.0535\n",
      "Mann-Whitney U, hybrid vs Flawed democracy: U = 1172, two-sided p = 0.0012\n",
      "Mann-Whitney U, hybrid vs Full democracy: U = 752, two-sided p = 0.0000\n",
      "Mann-Whitney U, hybrid vs all others: U = 3030, two-sided p = 0.00015\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "hybrid = countries.loc[countries[\"regime_2010\"] == \"Hybrid regime\", \"mean_abs_change\"]\n",
    "others = countries.loc[countries[\"regime_2010\"] != \"Hybrid regime\", \"mean_abs_change\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "diffs = [np.median(rng.choice(hybrid.values, len(hybrid))) - np.median(rng.choice(others.values, len(others)))\n",
    "         for _ in range(10000)]\n",
    "print(f\"hybrid median {hybrid.median():.3f} vs all others {others.median():.3f}; \"\n",
    "      f\"difference {hybrid.median() - others.median():.3f}, 95% bootstrap CI {np.percentile(diffs, [2.5, 97.5]).round(3)}\")\n",
    "print(\"full democracy median:\", round(summary.loc[\"Full democracy\", \"median\"], 3),\n",
    "      \"| hybrid / full ratio:\", round(hybrid.median() / summary.loc[\"Full democracy\", \"median\"], 1))\n",
    "\n",
    "for regime in [\"Authoritarian\", \"Flawed democracy\", \"Full democracy\"]:\n",
    "    other = countries.loc[countries[\"regime_2010\"] == regime, \"mean_abs_change\"]\n",
    "    test = stats.mannwhitneyu(hybrid, other, alternative=\"two-sided\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Mann-Whitney U, hybrid vs {regime}: U = {test.statistic:.0f}, two-sided p = {test.pvalue:.4f}\")\n",
    "test = stats.mannwhitneyu(hybrid, others, alternative=\"two-sided\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mann-Whitney U, hybrid vs all others: U = {test.statistic:.0f}, two-sided p = {test.pvalue:.5f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6cf54839",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Direction: is the extra movement up or down?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "d1d27f81",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-16T00:08:09.104572Z",
